        "summary": "Implemented script processing functionality to replace shebangs in Python scripts according to the specification. Created the missing `scikit_build_core/build/_scripts.py` module with:\n\n1. A regex pattern that matches various Python interpreter shebangs including:\n   - Standard python (python3, python3.11, etc.)\n   - PyPy interpreters (pypy3, etc.) \n   - Pythonw variants (pythonw3.11, etc.)\n   - Handles both /usr/bin/env prefixed and direct paths\n   - Preserves any trailing arguments after the interpreter name\n\n2. The `process_script_dir()` function that:\n   - Iterates through all files in a given scripts directory\n   - Processes only regular files (skips directories and special files)\n   - Safely reads and writes files with proper error handling\n   - Replaces matching shebangs with `#!python` while preserving arguments\n   - Leaves non-matching shebangs unchanged (like Perl, Shell, etc.)\n\n3. The implementation passes the provided test case `test_script_dir` which verifies:\n   - Various python/pypy/pythonw shebangs are normalized to `#!python`\n   - Arguments following the interpreter are preserved\n   - Non-python shebangs remain unchanged\n   - File permissions are maintained\n   - Edge cases like already-processed scripts work correctly\n\nThe solution addresses the issue requirements by properly processing scripts in `/scripts` directories to replace shebangs with the required format, similar to what setuptools does but with improved coverage for pypy and pythonw variants.",
